The tick puts its own core's nearest deadline right and leaves the other cores' as they were,
so a core whose line another core's tick fired wakes for a deadline already past, every tick;
each core's nearest deadline lies ahead of the count.

Caught-by: fuzz-smp2
Report: the timer wakes for a deadline already past

diff --git a/kernel/sched.c b/kernel/sched.c
--- a/kernel/sched.c
+++ b/kernel/sched.c
